.TH CASK\-VERIFY 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 6b26b19a" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
cask\-verify \- Verify (and safely extract) a signed Sealed Cask against trusted build keys.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cask\-verify
verify|extract \-\-cask FILE \-\-pubkey KEY [\-\-pubkey OLD] [\-\-dest DIR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify (and safely extract) a signed Sealed Cask against trusted build keys.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B verify \-\-cask FILE \-\-pubkey KEY
check the cask's seal; more \-\-pubkey for keys still trusted
.TP
.B extract \-\-cask FILE \-\-pubkey KEY \-\-dest DIR
verify, then extract into a new directory
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit codes: 0 verified, 1 refused, 2 usage or unreadable key.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
